==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Kaijin Doge]]s (1,800%) spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Imperator Sael]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*1 [[Madam Peng]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Bun Bun Symbiote]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Madam Peng]]s spawn, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
**20 [[Kaijin Doge]]s (200%) spawn, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
**2 [[Malizabeth]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
It is recommended to collect all [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] from [[Into the Future]] Chapter 1, 2, & 3 before attempting this stage. [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]] will be your best friend here, as his Strong Against Alien ability comes in real handy against Bun Bun Symbiote. Stack a few on Emperator Sael and watch them wreak havoc on the rest of the stage. Bring [[Goggles Cat (Special Cat)|Green Nyanko Ranger]], [[Scarf Cat (Special Cat)|Red Nyanko Ranger]], and [[Ribbon Cat (Special Cat)|Pink Nyanko Ranger]] to deal with the Kaijin supports. You want to specifically save Red Nyanko Ranger for Malizabeth, since she's really tanky.

